From bdcbae59669f5755d07292129e609586e803f209 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:50:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: one refused proxy dial skips the exit's other
 members for the request

What changed: when a candidate's proxy refuses the connection itself
(failProxy, a 502 saying proxyconnect/socks connect), the rest of the
request skips the members whose own request would really go out through
that same exit - the proxy netproxy.Resolve names for the member's base
URL and proxy choice - instead of dialling the same dead listener once
per member. A member that goes direct (loopback, the user's own network,
NO_PROXY, a direct setting) is never skipped, whatever its ProxyChoice
says: the choice "" only means "follows the global setting", and under a
dead global proxy a loopback member (Ollama, LM Studio) or one on the
LAN shares no exit with the member that failed. netproxy.Resolve is the
one decision Func and Dispatch's per-proxy transports both make, so the
key the sharing uses and the dial a request makes cannot drift. Such a
failure is no same-one retry of the last one left either, and nobody is
set aside: the next request dials the proxy again, so recovery keeps the
pace #381 gave it. A group that shares one dead proxy had asked every
member in turn and then retried the last with backoff - eight attempts
over 796 seconds in the report - each try refused at the same listener.

Run: TestProxyDownSkipsSharedProxy, TestProxyDownGlobalLeavesALoopback-
MemberDirect, TestProxyDownAsksAMemberOnItsOwnProxy, TestProxyDownLast-
NotRetried and TestProxyDownDistinctProxiesLastNotRetried are red with
the product change taken back out (the shared member dialled again, the
last retried with backoff), green with it; the loopback test was red
against the choice-keyed first draft (its member skipped through the
"" key) before the exit key. -race -count=3 green. Ablation: gateway.go
and fallback.go restored to upstream/main with the tests kept, four of
them fail again. TestResolveNamesTheRealProxy pins netproxy's decision
(loopback direct even with a proxy of its own) and fails with the
loopback guard taken out. Targeted regression (proxy, account-proxy,
plugin-proxy, agent-gone, patience, replan, retry, sink, lane, fallback,
first-token families) green. gofmt -l clean. go vet ./... (the known
trayimage cgo warning), linux/windows vet and darwin/linux/windows
builds green.

