ren't taken either. While the budget lasts, the last candidate's failure is held (`newHoldWriter`), and a streaming agent is kept alive through the pause with SSE comments (`pauseAlive`). The try is traced with `Again` (the pause), `Replan` (how many are asked again) and `Patience` (the budget in seconds). The group editor's "Every member busy" row sets it. A plain provider keeps only the same-one retries `passing` gives the last one left. An agent that goes away in either pause (the same-one retry's or a group's replan) ends the request there with 499: nobody is asked again, and the try whose pause it was is marked `Gone` (#1894, heng91: a relay down while its proxy was off, the agent's window closed). The Routing page says the agent canceled the request before the retry and lists it as canceled, rather than ending its story on "tried again in 2s", a retry that never came (`TestAgentGoneInTheRetryPause`, `routing-agent-gone.test.cjs`). A try that answered is recorded (`served`, `answered`) for routing, affinity and usage. A try is added to the route's `Tries` only as it is asked, so a later try is the record that the gateway went on from this one, and the Routing page tells what came of a try from that, never from where it stood in the order (#2281, xishuchkui-code: an Antigravity 502 empty reply that went on to the next account was told as "an error another account wouldn't fix, so Claude Code gets it"). The one case the record can't show is the last try left out of its allowance after an earlier failure that wasn't one, where the agent is told the earlier error: that try is marked `Earlier` (`routing-went-on.test.cjs`).
